## What it shows
The 50, 150 and 200-day simple moving averages on the price chart, a checklist table and a green shade behind every bar where all eight points of Mark Minervini's trend template pass:
- the close is above the 150 and 200-day averages;
- the 150-day is above the 200-day;
- the 200-day is higher than it was **SMA 200 rising over (bars)** ago (20 by default, about a month);
- the 50-day is above both the 150 and the 200-day;
- the close is above the 50-day;
- the close is at least **Above 52-week low by at least (%)** (30 by default) above the 52-week low;
- the close is within **Within 52-week high by (%)** (25 by default) of the 52-week high;
- the stock's return over the last year beats the **Benchmark**'s (NIFTY 50 by default).

The last point stands in for Minervini's RS rating, which ranks a stock against the whole market; here the stock is compared with one index. The table marks each point ✓ or ✗ at the latest bar, shows the number behind it and counts how many pass; the count is also in the Data Window as **Criteria passed**.

**Show the averages** (on by default) draws the three moving averages; turn it off to keep only the checklist and shading. **Shade bars that pass** (on by default) draws the green shade behind bars where all eight points pass. **Show the checklist** (on by default) draws the table; **Checklist position** (top right by default) places it on the chart.

## How to read it
- A stock that passes all eight is in what Minervini calls a stage 2 uptrend, the stage his setups are traded from; the template is a filter, not an entry signal.
- A count of six or seven shows a stock close to qualifying; check which point is missing.
- Alerts are available for **Trend template passed** and **Trend template lost**, each on the bar the state changes.

## Limits
- It needs a full year of daily bars (**Year (bars)**, 252 by default) before every point can be judged; a point that cannot be judged yet counts as not passing.
- Without the benchmark's data the relative strength point shows a dash and the template cannot pass.
- The averages count bars, so the template reads as intended on a daily chart only.
